{
 "_about": "GSTR-9 / GSTR-9C canonical layer (spec: docs/GSTR9_CANONICAL_SPEC.md). Both are the government's own Excel export: one sheet per Item / Part (names truncated to 31 characters, so a sheet is found by the leading words listed under 'sheets'; the first sheet whose name starts with any of them). Inside a sheet the original located every figure by its ROW LABEL (the text in column B - or column A for GSTR-9 Part I - must contain all the 'frags', case-insensitive, within the first 60 rows; 'occurrence' picks the n-th such row) and then took the numbers from fixed columns of that row (Taxable value / Central / State / Integrated / Cess, or Payable / Paid, depending on the Item). The canonical FACTS sheet keeps, per fact, the matched row's label, source sheet and row number and the numbers of its first eight columns (c0..c7); the reader takes the same columns the original did. 'kv' = the Part I label / value rows (rules: 'startswith' + 'contains' on the label for GSTR-9, exact label 'equals' for GSTR-9C); 'lists' = 'letters' (rows whose first cell is one of the letters, numbers from columns C and D - the Item 19 late-fee rows) or 'reasons' (the auditor's typed reason lines: column C text on rows whose first cell is alphabetic). 'note_if_missing' is informational only.",
